From fe623857d5bbabee51fa5393be030bf65335b924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:21:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] RvFileDialog: no size grip on Wayland (it covered the
 Open button's corner)

The file dialog enables QDialog's size grip. QDialog places it as a 17x17
child in the bottom-right corner, raised above the layout, and the style
sheet's `QWidget { background-color: rgb(50,50,50) }` rule makes it paint an
opaque square (QStyleSheetStyle CE_SizeGrip with a background but no image:
no grip glyph). The dialog layout's right/bottom margins are only 8 px, so
the grip covers a 9x9 px corner of the rightmost button (Open/Save) and also
takes the clicks there.

Measured with a -pyeval probe: grip (980,463 17x17), Open button right 989,
bottom 472 (Wayland); the same overlap exists on xcb with Qt 6 and in the
original Qt 5 build, so it is an upstream bug, not a Wayland one.

On Wayland the decoration (libadwaita / bradient plugin) or the compositor
already provides the resize edges, so do not create the grip there. X11 keeps
the grip (unchanged behaviour).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvFileDialog.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvFileDialog.cpp b/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvFileDialog.cpp
index ff1a7bc..18c9c72 100644
--- a/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvFileDialog.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/app/RvCommon/RvFileDialog.cpp
@@ -179,7 +179,10 @@ namespace Rv
         m_ui.autoRefreshCheckbox->setCheckState((m_allowAutoRefresh) ? Qt::Checked : Qt::Unchecked);
 
         setWindowTitle("Select Files/Directories");
-        setSizeGripEnabled(true);
+        // The size grip is a 17x17 child in the bottom-right corner, painted opaque by the style sheet's QWidget background rule.
+        // The layout's right/bottom margins are only 8 px, so it covers a 9x9 corner of the Open/Save button (and catches clicks
+        // there). On Wayland the window decoration / compositor already provides the resize edges, so do not create it there.
+        setSizeGripEnabled(!QGuiApplication::platformName().startsWith(QLatin1String("wayland")));
         m_reloadTimer = new QTimer(this);
         m_sidePanelTimer = new QTimer(this);
         m_columnViewTimer = new QTimer(this);
